      "copybook": "TRANREC",
      "level": 1,
      "name": "TRAN-RECORD",
      "start": 1,
      "length": 80,
      "category": "group",
      "description": "TRANREC: DAILY TRANSACTION FILE RECORD, 80 BYTES ONE HEADER, THE DETAILS, ONE TRAILER, TOLD APART BY THE RECORD TYPE. THE BODY IS REDEFINED FOR EACH RECORD TYPE. THE TRAILER CARRIES THE SENDER'S CONTROL TOTALS: THE DETAIL COUNT, THE SUM OF AMOUNTS AND THE SUM OF ACCOUNT NUMBERS. A TRANSFER (TR) NAMES THE ACCOUNT IT GOES TO. POSTING SPLITS IT IN TWO: THE DEBIT ON THE SENDING ACCOUNT, THEN A TRANSFER CREDIT (TC) ON THE RECEIVING ONE. A CREDIT THAT CANNOT POST GOES BACK AS A RETURNED TRANSFER (RT). TC AND RT ARE MADE BY POSTING, NEVER RECEIVED IN THE DAILY FILE. MODIFICATION HISTORY DATE       BY  CHANGE 1987-03-12 JA  ORIGINAL VERSION. 1991-06-03 PK  CR-0117 ACCOUNT NUMBER HASH IN THE TRAILER. 1996-04-15 PK  CR-0233 TRANSFERS: COUNTER ACCOUNT, FROM THE FILLER.",
